      "date": "2026-11-17 15:25:49.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 4:\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nLooks good; no need to re-spin. (suggestion) If the patch is refreshed for another reason, consider adding a sanity-lnet case for the two paths this changes. conf-sanity 73c only gets faster, it does not fail without the fix. One case could put an LNet delay rule on the Push PUT to a peer and check that `lnetctl net add` returns well within the LND timeout. The other could delay a ping REPLY, run `net add` so an old ping MD is still busy, then run `lnetctl lnet unconfigure`. That exercises the new wait on `ln_ping_target_mds` in lnet_ping_target_fini() and the lnet_assert_handler_unused() check after it.",
